            "text": "{\n  \"study_topic_id\": \"study-36b1f6ba12f5656d7176\",\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"text\": \"The absolute value function, written f(x)=|x|, assigns each real input its distance from zero, so its output is never negative. Its piecewise rule is f(x)=-x for x<0 and f(x)=x for x≥0: negative inputs are reflected to positive outputs, while zero stays zero. The graph is a V with its corner at (0,0), and it is symmetric about the y-axis. The function remains continuous at the corner, but it is not differentiable there because its left- and right-hand slopes differ. Away from zero, the slope is -1 on the left and +1 on the right. This makes absolute value useful for describing distance without direction.\",\n    \"source_urls\": [\n      \"https://openstax.org/books/college-algebra/pages/3-6-absolute-value-functions\",\n      \"https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Calculus/Calculus_3e_%28Apex%29/02%3A_Derivatives/2.01%3A_Instantaneous_Rates_of_Change-_The_Derivative\",\n      \"https://math.libretexts.org/Workbench/Elementary_Calculus%3A_An_Infinitesimal_Approach_%28Keisler%29/03%3A_Continuous_Functions/3.4%3A_Continuity\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"For x<0, |x|=-x; for x≥0, |x|=x.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://openstax.org/books/college-algebra/pages/3-6-absolute-value-functions\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The function is defined for all real inputs and has range [0, ∞).\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-1/pages/1-1-review-of-functions\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Its graph has a corner at the origin and is symmetric about the y-axis.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://openstax.org/books/college-algebra/pages/3-6-absolute-value-functions\",\n        \"https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-1/pages/1-1-review-of-functions\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The derivative is -1 for x<0 and +1 for x>0; it does not exist at x=0.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Calculus/Calculus_3e_%28Apex%29/02%3A_Derivatives/2.01%3A_Instantaneous_Rates_of_Change-_The_Derivative\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Although it is not differentiable at zero, the function is continuous there.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://math.libretexts.org/Workbench/Elementary_Calculus%3A_An_Infinitesimal_Approach_%28Keisler%29/03%3A_Continuous_Functions/3.4%3A_Continuity\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"3.6 Absolute Value Functions - College Algebra\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openstax.org/books/college-algebra/pages/3-6-absolute-value-functions\",\n      \"publisher\": \"OpenStax\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-24T18:42:11.188461+00:00\",\n      \"supports\": \"Defines absolute value as distance from zero, gives its piecewise rule, and describes the graph's corner and distance applications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"1.1 Review of Functions - Calculus Volume 1\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-1/pages/1-1-review-of-functions\",\n      \"publisher\": \"OpenStax\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-24T18:42:11.188461+00:00\",\n      \"supports\": \"Provides the piecewise definition, nonnegative range, and symmetry about the y-axis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"2.1: Instantaneous Rates of Change- The Derivative - Calculus 3e (Apex)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Calculus/Calculus_3e_%28Apex%29/02%3A_Derivatives/2.01%3A_Instantaneous_Rates_of_Change-_The_Derivative\",\n      \"publisher\": \"Mathematics LibreTexts\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-24T18:42:11.188461+00:00\",\n      \"supports\": \"Derives the slopes on either side of zero and explains why the derivative does not exist at zero.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"3.4: Continuity - Elementary Calculus: An Infinitesimal Approach\",\n      \"url\": \"https://math.libretexts.org/Workbench/Elementary_Calculus%3A_An_Infinitesimal_Approach_%28Keisler%29/03%3A_Continuous_Functions/3.4%3A_Continuity\",\n      \"publisher\": \"Mathematics LibreTexts\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-24T18:42:11.188461+00:00\",\n      \"supports\": \"States and demonstrates that the absolute value function is continuous but not differentiable at zero.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"research_queries\": [\n    \"site:openstax.org absolute value function definition graph\",\n    \"site:math.libretexts.org absolute value function derivative not differentiable zero\",\n    \"site:encyclopediaofmath.org absolute value function modulus real number\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The overview is one original paragraph of 99 words. Each overview claim and key fact has one or more directly opened source URLs.\",\n  \"unresolved_concerns\": [],\n  \"self_check_complete\": true\n}"
